# "When this creature dies, exile it and create ten tapped Treasure tokens": "it" is the card put into the graveyard, and
# only while it is still there (CR 400.7, 608.2h); the Treasures do not depend on it. Bot2's Baleful Strix (deathtouch)
# attacks Bot1, its damage is dealt to Ancient Adamantoise instead and destroys it. With the dies trigger on the stack,
# Bot2 exiles the Adamantoise card from Bot1's graveyard with Deathrite Shaman (and gains 2 life). The trigger then finds
# no card to exile and still makes the ten tapped Treasures for Bot1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Forest
Forest
Forest
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Baleful Strix
Forest
Deathrite Shaman
Forest
Forest
Forest x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot2.Choose()
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Baleful Strix.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Deathrite Shaman.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Attack(Baleful Strix)
Bot2.Battlefield.Deathrite Shaman.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Ancient Adamantoise; Ability: creature)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 22
Exile = Ancient Adamantoise
Bot1.Graveyard = Show and Tell; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 12
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#10.Tapped = true
